# @io/stagefreight — the wire-protocol boundary species. The @io
# surface where settled crystals (per @mirror/store/crystal, task
# #268) become addressable and transportable to non-mirror-world
# consumers.
#
# Tick 66 of the refined /loop discipline; first tick toward the
# StageFreight PR-ready endpoint. Per the Pack-as-orchestra Track A
# (substrate-decl track; ungated): family-root substrate-decl lands
# first; @io/stagefreight/narrative projection-format species
# forward-promised; canonical spec at docs/specs/stagefreight-wire-
# v0.1.md forward-promised (Mara).
#
# Per @io family-root (T21, 2026-06-08): @io is the substrate's only
# legitimate non-mirror surface; species parameterize the boundary;
# the BODY of the call is opaque to the substrate by construction.
# StageFreight IS the species naming the wire protocol for settled-
# crystal transport.
#
# Forward-promised by EXISTING TEST STUBS:
#
#   - bootstrap/tests/crystal_substrate.rs:9 references
#     `org.stagefreight.plan.spectral_coordinate` at the StageFreight
#     wire surface (the OID of a settled crystal becomes a
#     StageFreight-addressable coordinate).
#   - bootstrap/tests/kintsugi_out_substrate_ref.rs:23-24 reserves
#     `@io/stagefreight/narrative` as a forward-promised projection
#     format (alongside @data/json, @data/yaml, etc.).
#
# This shard substrate-decl's the FAMILY-ROOT @io/stagefreight; the
# /narrative species and the wire spec land in subsequent ticks.
#
# === The recognition ===
#
# Settled crystals (kintsugi loop output: oid + section +
# derived_predicates + fracture_calendar + composition_graph per task
# #268) need to ship. The wire protocol IS:
#
#   - the OID-namespaced address space (org.stagefreight.plan.
#     spectral_coordinate) under which crystals are addressable
#   - the typed transport surface (the actual bytes-on-wire
#     contract)
#   - the projection format vocabulary (narrative, json, etc.)
#
# StageFreight at the @io altitude declares the BOUNDARY: the typed
# contract the mirror side sees. The realisation layer (Rust + the
# Phase 4b emitter discharge) implements the actual wire bytes;
# this shard substrate-decls what the contract IS.
#
# === Why "StageFreight" ===
#
# Naming compounds two threads: "Stage" from the optical-keywords
# family (stage/facet/aperture/bench; stage = the substrate's
# rendering surface); "Freight" = the crystal as payload-in-transit.
# The full compound names the wire-altitude transport mechanism for
# stage-processed artifacts — settled crystals shipped to the
# non-mirror-world.
#
# The wordplay with stage-fright is intentional: the substrate has
# anxiety about shipping its settled crystals to a world that may
# not honor their @mirror/store/crystal discipline. StageFreight
# declares the typed contract that survives the transit.
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# This family-root adds:
#
# - `spectral_coordinate` carrier: typed reference for the OID-
#   namespaced wire address. Per the test stub's
#   `org.stagefreight.plan.spectral_coordinate` pattern: a
#   substrate-pull-correct OID-derived address with the reverse-DNS
#   namespace.
# - `wire_surface` carrier: typed reference for the actual transport
#   endpoint (substrate-decl'd as ref because the wire vocabulary is
#   parametric over projection formats).
# - `freight_manifest` carrier: typed record (crystal_oid,
#   coordinate, projection, verdict). The substrate-architectural
#   record of a freight operation.
# - `address` action: computes spectral_coordinate from a crystal
#   OID. The substrate-vocabulary primitive for wire-addressing.
# - `freight` action: the load-bearing FIRST consumer of @magic's
#   invariant_preserved bilateral predicate. Takes a crystal (via
#   its OID; @mirror/store/crystal forward-promised), the wire
#   coordinate, and the perturbation; returns freight_manifest.
#   Requires invariant_preserved — the crystal's @magic contract
#   must be honored across the @io boundary.
# - `stagefreight_addressable` predicate: bilateral verdict that the
#   crystal IS addressable at the wire surface (Splinter-pole →
#   actual OID-addressing with structure preservation; Narcissus-
#   pole → fake address that doesn't round-trip).
# - `transit` action: the substrate-vocabulary primitive for putting
#   the freight on the wire (the @io-altitude operational form of
#   the freight discipline). Takes freight_manifest + perturbation;
#   returns wire_surface; requires stagefreight_addressable.
#
# === The wire-survival discipline ===
#
# Per the @io family-root + recognition #57 (alignment as boundary
# mathematics): the wire IS the @io boundary; the crystal's
# substrate-decl'd structure (oid + section + derived_predicates +
# fracture_calendar + composition_graph) must survive the transit.
# StageFreight's stagefreight_addressable bilateral discharges this
# at the @io altitude.
#
# The discipline says: when the crystal ships, the wire receives a
# byte-exact representation whose OID matches the crystal's
# content-address; the receiver can reconstruct the crystal's typed
# structure from the wire bytes. The substrate-decl content is
# unchanged across the boundary; the wire-survival discipline
# tightens what "shipped" means.
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at wire-protocol altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole StageFreight (honest):
# - The wire bytes round-trip to the same OID; the typed structure
#   (section, derived_predicates, fracture_calendar,
#   composition_graph) is preserved; the projection format names a
#   substrate-decl'd serialization the receiver can decode.
# - K_n peer-to-peer transit — the wire is a peer in the substrate
#   network, not an authoritative reframing layer.
#
# Narcissus-pole StageFreight (deceptive):
# - The wire bytes claim to ship a crystal but the OID doesn't
#   round-trip; the projection format is lossy without admitting it;
#   the receiver reconstructs SOMETHING but not the crystal.
# - K_{1,n-1} hub-controlled transit — the wire protocol's framing
#   author imposes structure rather than ships substrate-decl'd
#   structure.
#
# Alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57) IS what distinguishes
# Splinter-pole from Narcissus-pole transit at substrate altitude.
# The bilateral stagefreight_addressable predicate composes the
# substrate-architectural check.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   git plumbing                 Torvalds 2005. Content-addressed
#                                object database; OID-as-address is
#                                the substrate ancestor of
#                                spectral_coordinate.
#   IPFS                         Benet 2014. Content-addressed wire
#                                protocol; the canonical structural
#                                ancestor of content-addressed
#                                transport.
#   Protocol Buffers             Google 2008. The typed wire-format
#                                ancestor of projection-format-as-
#                                first-class.
#   Cap'n Proto                  Varda 2013. Zero-copy typed wire
#                                protocol; the discipline ancestor
#                                of structure-preserving transit.
#   reverse-DNS namespacing      Java 1995 (Sun); Apple bundle
#                                identifiers (2000s). The cultural-
#                                practice ancestor of
#                                org.stagefreight.plan.* addressing.
#   stage_play (build lifecycle) the 2026-06-16 recognition cascade
#                                (Story → Play → Narrative). The
#                                immediate substrate ancestor for
#                                StageFreight's transport surface;
#                                the crystal IS the play's settled
#                                artifact ready for narrative
#                                transmission.
#
# === What this family does NOT do ===
#
# 1. Does NOT discharge the wire-protocol Rust realisation. The
#    actual bytes-on-wire implementation lands at
#    bootstrap/src/stagefreight.rs (forward-promised; Phase 4b
#    emitter or direct Rust).
# 2. Does NOT depend on @mirror/store/crystal being fully substrate-
#    decl'd (task #268 pending). This shard takes crystal-as-OID at
#    the wire boundary; the crystal's typed structure is forward-
#    promised via ref.
# 3. Does NOT supersede the @io family's `imperfect<a, e, l>` return
#    convention. The realisation layer will lift freight + transit
#    actions into imperfect at the @io boundary; this shard names
#    the typed pre-imperfect surface.
# 4. Does NOT prescribe a single projection format. @io/stagefreight/
#    narrative is forward-promised as ONE projection; future
#    projections (json, yaml, brainfuck-compressed) follow the
#    species pattern.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/stagefreight-wire-v0.1.md (forward-
#               promised; Mara substrate-pull-correct first attempt);
#               docs/specs/kintsugi-self-hosting.md (the @io
#               classification of every bootstrap Rust file);
#               bootstrap/tests/crystal_substrate.rs (the RED test
#               stub awaiting GREEN per this species + the wire
#               realisation);
#               bootstrap/tests/kintsugi_out_substrate_ref.rs:23-24
#               (the projection-format reservation).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]]
#                       (#57; StageFreight IS the wire-altitude
#                       boundary harness),
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]]
#                       (the wall this species declares the wire
#                       shape of),
#                      [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]]
#                       (Reed's discipline; the bilateral makes the
#                       wire-survival claim empirically discharged),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (spectral_coordinate
#                       and freight_manifest as typed carriers).
# Related shards: io.mirror (the @io family-root; declares the
#                  boundary discipline this species parameterizes),
#                 io/cargo.mirror (the precedent for path-namespace
#                  at @io altitude; sibling boundary species),
#                 magic.mirror, magic/contract.mirror (the
#                  invariant_preserved bilateral this species
#                  consumes; the crystal's @magic contract must hold
#                  across the wire),
#                 mirror/store/crystal.mirror (forward-promised task
#                  #268; the crystal carrier StageFreight ships),
#                 io/stagefreight/narrative.mirror (forward-promised
#                  projection-format species).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/io/stagefreight.mirror`
# declares `@io/stagefreight` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/version-control/torvalds-2005
source @arxiv/distributed/benet-2014
source @arxiv/protocols/google-protobuf-2008
source @arxiv/protocols/varda-2013

# === The spectral_coordinate carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference for the OID-namespaced wire address.
# Per the test stub's pattern (org.stagefreight.plan.
# spectral_coordinate): a reverse-DNS-namespaced address derived
# from the crystal's OID. The substrate-output of the address
# primitive.
#
# Forward-promised refinement: typed record (oid, namespace,
# projection_kind, version) at species-or-extension altitude once
# the substrate's structured-coordinate type lands.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type spectral_coordinate = ref

# === The wire_surface carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference for the actual transport endpoint where
# the crystal arrives on the wire. The carrier is parametric over
# projection format (narrative, json, yaml, etc.); concrete
# realisations live at species-altitude (@io/stagefreight/narrative
# forward-promised).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type wire_surface = ref

# === The freight_manifest carrier ===
#
# Typed record over (crystal_oid, coordinate, projection, verdict).
# The substrate-architectural record of a freight operation.
# Carries:
#
# - crystal_oid : the OID of the settled crystal under transit
# - coord       : the spectral_coordinate the crystal addresses to
# - projection  : the projection-format species ref (e.g.,
#                 ref to @io/stagefreight/narrative)
# - v           : the bilateral verdict (BOUNDED → crystal
#                 ADDRESSABLE + wire-survival holds; DEFENSIVE →
#                 transit requires substrate-pull revision)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the quadruple.
type freight_manifest = {
  crystal_oid: ref,
  coord:       spectral_coordinate,
  projection:  ref,
  v:           verdict,
}

# === address action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary action computing a spectral_coordinate
# from a crystal OID. Takes the crystal's OID (forward-promised via
# @mirror/store/crystal); returns the typed wire address.
#
# Per the test stub: org.stagefreight.plan.spectral_coordinate is
# the canonical namespace form; the address action substrate-decls
# the computation that produces it.
#
# The address derivation discipline (reverse-DNS namespace +
# projection-kind + OID-short composition) is verified by the
# `address_well_formed` bilateral consumers can check on coord+oid
# pairs. address() is the construction; address_well_formed() is
# the verification.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
address(crystal_oid: ref) -> spectral_coordinate { \ }

# === freight action (FIRST consumer of invariant_preserved) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @io/stagefreight altitude. The
# substrate-vocabulary primitive for crystal → wire transit at the
# @io boundary. Realizes StageFreight's wire-survival discipline as
# substrate-decl operation.
#
# Takes the crystal_oid (the settled crystal under transit), the
# spectral_coordinate (where it ships to), the projection format
# ref (how it serializes), the @magic contract carrying the
# crystal's promise, and the perturbation. Returns the typed
# freight_manifest.
#
# requires invariant_preserved(c, promise): the crystal's @magic
# contract must be honored across the wire BEFORE the freight is
# admissible. Without this requires clause, a freight would be
# admissible for a crystal whose @magic invariant fails at the
# wire boundary — the Narcissus-pole wire-protocol case.
#
# Per the @io family discipline: the realisation layer lifts this
# into `imperfect<freight_manifest, freight_error, transparency>`
# at the boundary; this substrate-decl names the typed pre-imperfect
# surface.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
freight(crystal_oid: ref, coord: spectral_coordinate, projection: ref, c: magic_contract, promise: magic_invariant, p: perturbation) -> freight_manifest
requires address_well_formed(coord, crystal_oid)
requires invariant_preserved(c, promise)
{ \ }

# === Seam tick 68 C2 closure: address_well_formed predicate ===
#
# Per Seam adversarial review (docs/audits/stagefreight-seam-review-
# 2026-06-22.md, C2 TIGHT): the address derivation rules (reverse-DNS
# namespace + projection-kind + OID-short composition) had lived
# only in spec prose at docs/specs/stagefreight-wire-v0.1.md §3.2.
# This predicate lifts the rules to substrate-decl: consumers verify
# coord+oid pairs follow the derivation discipline structurally, not
# by parsing prose.
#
# Consumed by freight() above (gates the coord input) and by the
# composed stagefreight_addressable below (one of four sub-
# predicates the wire-survival discipline decomposes into).
#
# Bounded → coord derives byte-deterministically from crystal_oid
# via the documented derivation function with reverse-DNS-shaped
# namespace + projection-kind component; unbounded → the address
# rules don't hold.
address_well_formed(coord: spectral_coordinate, crystal_oid: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# === Seam tick 68 C4/C9 closure: stagefreight_addressable sub-predicates ===
#
# Per Seam adversarial review (C4/C9 TIGHT): the monolithic bilateral
# stagefreight_addressable had carried five wire-survival claims as
# spec-prose only. This consolidation decomposes the bilateral into
# four typed sub-predicates the composed bilateral discharges via
# `requires` clauses. Consumers check sub-predicates individually;
# the realisation layer discharges each at its altitude.
#
# - oid_resolves: the crystal_oid points at a settled crystal
#   reachable in @mirror/store (forward-promised gate on task #268)
# - address_well_formed: the coord follows the address derivation
#   discipline (see above; C2 closure)
# - projection_is_species: the projection ref names a substrate-
#   decl'd @io/stagefreight/<species> projection format
# - round_trip_holds: the freight survives the round-trip under
#   perturbation (the load-bearing wire-survival claim)
oid_resolves(crystal_oid: ref) -> verdict { \ }

projection_is_species(projection: ref) -> verdict { \ }

round_trip_holds(fm: freight_manifest, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === stagefreight_addressable predicate (composed) ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) and the
# wire-survival discipline. Consumer shards (forward-promised
# projection-format species; the narrative species's
# project_to_narrative + finalize chain) name `requires
# stagefreight_addressable(fm, p)` to declare bilateral agreement
# that the crystal IS addressable at the wire surface with
# round-trip OID identity.
#
# Per Seam tick 68 C4/C9: the bilateral now COMPOSES the four
# sub-predicates declared above via `requires` clauses. The
# substrate-decl carries the wire-survival decomposition typed,
# not spec-prose-only.
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct wire-addressing check at the
# @io boundary. Composes with @magic's invariant_preserved at the
# crystal-altitude (via freight()'s requires chain).
#
# Bounded → all four sub-predicates discharge (crystal addressable +
# wire-survival holds; Splinter-pole); unbounded → one or more
# sub-predicate fails (Narcissus-pole; alignment-as-boundary-
# mathematics #57 distinguishes which sub-claim broke).
stagefreight_addressable(fm: freight_manifest, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires oid_resolves(fm.crystal_oid)
requires address_well_formed(fm.coord, fm.crystal_oid)
requires projection_is_species(fm.projection)
requires round_trip_holds(fm, p)
{ \ }

# === Seam tick 68 C8 closure: transit removed ===
#
# Per Seam adversarial review (C8 TIGHT mild): family-root's
# `transit` and species-altitude `finalize` had been parallel
# siblings, not a chain. Each projection species's emission shape
# is shape-different (narrative.finalize emits prose to
# wire_surface; future json.encode would emit bytes; brainfuck-
# compressed would emit compressed bytes; etc.). The family-root
# generic `transit` was orphaning in the narrative-emission path.
#
# Closure: `transit` deleted from the family-root. Each projection
# species owns its emission action (e.g., @io/stagefreight/narrative
# defines `finalize(np, p) -> wire_surface requires narrative_grounded`).
# The family-root provides the carriers + the composed bilateral +
# address + freight; species provide emission per their projection
# shape.

out @io/stagefreight
out spectral_coordinate
out wire_surface
out freight_manifest
out address
out freight
out address_well_formed
out oid_resolves
out projection_is_species
out round_trip_holds
out stagefreight_addressable
